---
import ProposalLayout from "../../layouts/ProposalLayout.astro";
import ProposalSection from "../../components/proposal/ProposalSection.astro";
import proposalData, { sections } from "../../data/proposals/sensorhubb";
import { Image } from "astro:assets";
import sensorhubbLogo from "../../images/sensorhubb-logo.avif";

export const proposal = proposalData;
---
<ProposalLayout proposal={proposal}>
  <a slot="clientLogo" href={proposal.clientUrl}>
    <Image src={sensorhubbLogo} alt="SensorHubb" class="w-[180px] h-auto" loading="eager" />
  </a>
  <ProposalSection slot="after-sitemap" id={sections.leadScoring.slug} heading={sections.leadScoring.text}>
    <p>We’ll replace the current contact-details form with a short, stepped booking flow that models your existing ICP scoring criteria in HubSpot. The aim is to turn your internal qualification process into a useful website journey—not introduce a new scoring system.</p>
    <ul>
      <li>Translate the guide into concise questions, conditional steps and eligibility checks, using your existing weights, thresholds and routing exceptions.</li>
      <li>Write responses, the provisional score and attribution to HubSpot, then route visitors to the appropriate booking, nurture or self-serve next step.</li>
      <li>Keep criteria that require a sales conversation separate from form-derived points, with rep confirmation recorded in HubSpot rather than assumed by the form.</li>
      <li>Confirm the question wording, field mapping and calendar handoffs with sales, and test each approved route before launch.</li>
    </ul>
  </ProposalSection>

</ProposalLayout>
